# MiniRust architecture

Stack: Rust, Tokio, Axum, Leptos SSR, Tailwind CSS, tracing, dotenvy. Planned later: MariaDB/SQLx, Redis, JWT, Teloxide. Do not take those dependencies unless the feature needs them.

Layout:

```text
apps/api          Axum REST
apps/web          Leptos SSR + Tailwind CSS UI
crates/config     env configuration
crates/core       domain types and AppError (no Axum/Leptos/SQLx/Redis)
crates/services   business logic shared by apps
```

Layering: UI (Leptos + Tailwind) → Handler → Application service → Domain (`core`) → Repository/adapter → Infrastructure.

- Handlers stay thin. Put rules in `crates/services`.
- `core` and `services` must not depend on Axum, Leptos, Tailwind CSS, MariaDB, SQLx, Redis, Teloxide, or vendor SDKs.
- `apps/web` owns presentation concerns. Tailwind CSS is the only CSS framework for the frontend.
- Do not add Bootstrap or another CSS/UI framework. Do not maintain Bootstrap compatibility.
- Prefer Tailwind utility classes and small reusable Leptos components over framework-specific CSS abstractions.
- Do not create empty speculative crates. Add `apps/bot`, `apps/worker`, or extra `crates/*` only when implementing that feature.
- MariaDB and Redis stay optional at startup. Redis is never the source of truth. Cache entries need a TTL when cache exists.
- Do not commit secrets. Do not log passwords or tokens.
- English identifiers, comments, and user-facing baseline strings.
- Do not commit, push, or open a PR unless the user asks.
